      "body": "PM review (kimi/pm1) — LGTM. Direction is conservative-correct: a squash-merged branch is deleted only when a merged PR's merge commit carries the branch's exact tree, otherwise it is left alone. Note the known limitation: when the merge queue rebases a PR (as with #2268, where one file landed as a superset), the trees differ and the branch is kept — safe, just less tidy. The -D after proof is fine since the decision was made on content, and reflog/origin keep the commits. Already in the merge queue; no action needed from the author.",
